      "name": "p-box-skin",
      "settings": {
        "bg_color": "#f9f9f9",
        "reverse": false,
        "text": "Select the hair and skin options that closely resemble your natural hair and skin colors.",
        "text1": "Choose your skin tone",
        "text2": "Choose your hair color",
        "text3": "* IPL technology works best on dark hair and fair skin. It is least effective on blonde, gray, and red hair and is not suitable for very dark skin.",
        "text4": "Is IPL right for you?",
        "text5": "IPL works by targeting melanin (pigment), so its effectiveness depends on the melanin levels in both the skin and hair. As a result, IPL may be less effective on lighter hair colors due to lower melanin levels, and it could pose safety concerns for darker skin tones, which absorb higher levels of energy due to their higher melanin content.",
        "text6": "Compatible.",
        "text7": "IPL is both safe and effective for the skin tone and hair color you have selected.",
        "text8": "Try again",
        "text9": "Not compatible.",
        "text10": "IPL is not compatible with your skin tone and hair color.",
        "text11": "Learn more",
        "text12": "Settings",
        "text13": "Sorry, IPL is not suitable for lighter hair colors.The effectiveness of IPL treatment depends on the amount of melanin present in the hair follicles. Light blonde, red, and gray hair may not contain sufficient melanin to be effectively treated with IPL.",
        "text14": "Sorry, IPL is not suitable for darker skin tones.IPL technology cannot differentiate between the melanin in the hair follicles and that in the skin. Darker skin tones, with their higher melanin content, can absorb higher energy levels, potentially raising safety concerns.",
        "text15": "IPL is not suitable for darker skin tones.",
        "text16": "Notice how the dark balloon burst? That's because it absorbed too much energy. IPL technology cannot differentiate between the melanin in the hair follicles and that in the skin. Darker skin tones, with their higher melanin content, can absorb higher energy levels, potentially raising safety concerns.",
        "text21": "IPL is not suitable for lighter hair colors.",
        "text22": "The effectiveness of IPL treatment depends on the amount of melanin present in the hair follicles. Just as the light pulses pass through the light-colored balloon without affecting it, blonde, red, and gray hair may not have sufficient melanin to be effectively treated with IPL.",
        "text17": "shopify://shop_images/6811a0dfef27c57904d52359c8e08c19.gif",
        "text20": "shopify://shop_images/6811a0dfef27c57904d52359c8e08c19.gif",
        "text18": "",
        "text19": "Settings",
        "text23": ""
